  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{5}{8}$ on the left and $\\frac{5}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/67dd516958b830c5442ab740683b23866c09e9422ac48c9259131f73870ae951.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $3$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $3$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right.  \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}÷3=\\frac{5}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$",
